tools.json contains the 100 application, compose, deployment, domain,
environment and project API definitions derived from @dokploy/mcp 0.30.7
(https://github.com/Dokploy/mcp), Copyright 2026 Dokploy Technologies, Inc.
The definitions were converted from Zod to JSON Schema; unsupported provider
regex constraints were removed. Runtime code was independently implemented.
The original attribution is preserved in LICENSE.dokploy.

Modifications (2026-11-13):
- OAuth client registration also accepts claude.ai callbacks and HTTP
  loopback callbacks (localhost / 127.0.0.1, RFC 8252) so Claude Code and
  claude.ai can sign in; the approval page's form-action CSP allows them.
- Refresh tokens use a sliding 90-day lifetime instead of a fixed 14 days.
- Six tool definitions in tools.json were updated to match the Dokploy
  v0.31.2 API (application-update, application-saveGithubProvider,
  application-readAppMonitoring, compose-update, project-update,
  environment-update).
